WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.687 position:63%
We are going up, I said we are going up.

00:00:02.687 --> 00:00:04.557 position:63%
We are going up, I said we are going up.

00:00:04.557 --> 00:00:07.080 position:56%
Forest Green are tantalizingly close

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.180 position:75%
to playing in the third tier of English football

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.903 position:56%
for the first time in their history.

00:00:10.903 --> 00:00:12.990
Being successful on the pitch

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.010 position:61%
absolutely strengthens our eco message,

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.710
because it gives us credibility

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.160
in the eyes of football fans.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.930
This is Forest Green Rovers,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.860 position:83%
UN-certified as carbon neutral, and described by FIFA

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.200 position:59%
as the world's greenest football club.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.380 position:72%
The mission became about reaching sports fans,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.240 position:81%
people that are passionate about a particular sport,

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.100 position:66%
in our case football, and making them fans

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.050 position:83%
of the environment as well, and we've seen that work.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.940
Our ethics and sustainability,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.710
we brought them here to the club.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.600 position:63%
Our fans come here, they see what we do,

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.540 position:81%
they go home and they start to change how they live.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.570 position:66%
Football has an added kind of opportunity,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.040
which I think is a responsibility,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.293 position:63%
to use its platform to influence people.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.350 position:56%
Thanks in large part to their owner,

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.600 position:70%
these minnows of the English game are proving

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.880
to have an outsized influence.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.800 position:63%
The season just passed saw the team play

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.480
in the Fourth Division.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.910 position:58%
That's about 70 teams below the likes

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.880 position:63%
of giants Manchester City and Liverpool.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.030 position:84%
But the team are on track for promotion to League One,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:20.030 position:88%
something never achieved in the club's 133-year history,

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.800 position:73%
and it could have an even greater impact thanks

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.133 position:88%
to the club's leadership in fighting the climate crisis.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.660
Based in the west of the country,

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.700 position:63%
Forest Green Rovers has become something

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.580 position:75%
of a passion project for the man often described

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.863
as a green energy industrialist.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.000
When I got here in August, 2010,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.670 line:0%
the club had 13 players, that was it.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.070 line:0%
Part-time, never trained on a full size pitch,

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.690 position:64%
so I helped them out, I thought, why not?

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.960 position:88%
Club was 120 years old, big part of its local community.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.047 position:56%
At the end of the summer, they said,

00:01:59.047 --> 00:02:00.930 position:88%
"You need to be in charge, you need to be the chairman."

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.270 position:56%
I was like, "Whoa, I'm really busy,"

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.520 position:92%
but they made it clear, it was that or the club would fold,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.410 position:59%
and so I thought about it and thought,

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.783
well, you know, how hard can it be?

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:11.760
I'll just run the football club.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.170
But I didn't think beyond that.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.973
I didn't think about anything.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.230
Vince is an outlier when it comes

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.503 position:91%
to business leaders, let alone the owner of a sports team.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.780
Dropping out of school,

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.150 position:61%
he joined a new age traveler community,

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.670 position:63%
where he tinkered with trucks to get by.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.540 position:89%
In 1985, he was caught up in the Battle of the Beanfield,

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.070
an assault by British police

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.456 position:63%
on travelers heading towards Stonehenge.

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:39.059
Get out. Open the door, then.

00:02:40.925 --> 00:02:42.257
Stop it. Just come out.

00:02:42.257 --> 00:02:44.850 position:72%
By the early '90s, he'd built a small windmill

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:48.960 position:91%
on his van, connected it to power lights and a water pump,

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.510 position:70%
and found himself on a hill above Nailsworth,

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.373
the home of Forest Green Rovers.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.220 position:80%
Because I had a windmill on the roof of my trailer,

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.390
I knew it was a windy spot,

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.740 position:64%
because you're in touch with those things

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.060 position:58%
when your energy comes from the wind.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.350 position:63%
You've got batteries, you've got meters,

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.060 position:59%
you see it come in, you see it go out.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.820 position:89%
You're in tune with what you use and where it comes from.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.610 position:94%
So I knew it was a windy hill, and then I just had this idea

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.290
that I could spend another 10 years

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.180 position:63%
living this low-impact lifestyle myself,

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.520 position:89%
or I could drop back in, try and build a bigger windmill,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.343
so I decided to do the second one.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.790 position:56%
Vince started a wind energy business

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.040
called Ecotricity.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.890 position:75%
Its success turned him into a multi-millionaire,

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.380 position:81%
and was instrumental in establishing renewable power

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.120
in the UK's energy mix.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.770
I mean, wind energy wasn't even 1%

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.990
in Britain at that point.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.520
And what are we now?

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.380 position:58%
Renewable energy combined, about 40%,

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.980
and most of that is wind energy.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.790
Transforming the energy landscape

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.940 position:78%
was the priority, but Vince was becoming conscious

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.310
that creating a more sustainable UK

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:50.640 position:84%
would require more holistic change in our daily lives.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.220 position:84%
I'm no Jeremy Clarkson, I want to be clear about that,

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.810
but I am a bit of a petrol head,

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.310
and I'm a tree hugger as well.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:57.840
I spend my life building windmills

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.900 position:80%
and fighting climate change, and driving fast cars.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:01.980
What am I gonna do about it?

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.600
It's a big contradiction.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.210 position:69%
It can't all be sandals and lentils, can it?

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.140
He went about building

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.950 position:77%
the UK's first electric vehicle charging network.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.330
More people would buy electric cars

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.800 position:61%
if there were more places to charge up,

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.840 position:67%
and people would build more charging points

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.160 position:56%
if more people bought electric cars,

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.470 position:83%
so we thought we'd jump in, build a national network,

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.240 position:59%
and try and get the whole thing going.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.670 position:70%
Then, he helped build an electric sports car,

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.380
the Nemesis.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.410 position:69%
Since then, he started a vegan food company,

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.150
and even produces diamonds made

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.703 position:64%
with carbon captured from the atmosphere.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.210
I got into energy in the '90s,

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.830
because the way the energy was made

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.630 position:78%
in Britain back then was the biggest single source

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.790 position:72%
of carbon emissions from burning fossil fuels.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.560 position:64%
This is where the mission now comes from,

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.390 position:86%
because we found that transport was the second biggest,

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:47.700 position:64%
and food was the third, and between them,

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.250 position:83%
they're 80% of everybody's personal carbon footprint,

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.920 position:91%
and that rule also applies to a football club of any size,

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.323 position:61%
a business, a whole country, basically.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.310 position:63%
And it was food that started the changes

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.720
at Forest Green Rovers.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.450 position:83%
Day one here of being in charge of the football club,

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.620
I bumped into my first thing.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.080 position:72%
We were serving a beef lasagna to our players,

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.770 position:88%
and I sat down immediately with the chef and the manager

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.240
and said, we can't do this,

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.160
so we took red meat off our menu

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.410
on day one of being in charge.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:19.350 position:84%
We upset some people, and we said, look, try our food,

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.640 position:58%
and this is why we do it, by the way,

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.350 position:61%
we didn't just do it, we explained why,

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.000 position:64%
and if you don't like what we serve here,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.750
just bring your own, we don't mind.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.160
I'm not vegan or vegetarian,

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.980 position:73%
but I don't mind not eating meat when I'm here,

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.920 line:0%
and I think quite a few people have recognized

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.230 line:0%
that they can eat meat any other time

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.000
of the day or the week.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.700 position:86%
Why not try vegan food and then be pleasantly surprised

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:42.650
that they enjoy it?

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.990
In the old days, you'd go up

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:46.920
and you'd get a cup of coffee,

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:49.920 position:77%
and somebody would say, do you want some of this,

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.930
and pull out a hip flask,

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:54.300 line:0%
and you'd think, I'm not quite sure,

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.590 line:0%
and they'd brought milk into the stadium,

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.930 line:0%
they'd brought cows milk into the stadium.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.900 position:66%
So those changes were quite hard, I think,

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.040 position:89%
and I think some of the fan base moved away from the club

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.150
as a consequence of that,

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:11.150 position:78%
but we've introduced a whole new set of supporters

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.633 position:91%
and followers who really like what the club stand for now.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.470 position:59%
Food sales have gone through the roof,

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:23.370 position:70%
the crowd growth has been phenomenal as well,

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:24.930 position:64%
and all of these were things that people,

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.400 position:61%
plenty of people, said wouldn't happen.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.810 position:59%
They said people won't come to a game;

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:28.920
if they do, they won't eat;

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:29.970
they'll bankrupt the club.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:32.100 position:91%
All this kind of stuff, so there was plenty of skepticism,

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.440 position:75%
but I didn't ever doubt it would work, actually.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.580
I didn't really care either,

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.670 position:83%
because I couldn't run a football club that broke all

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:42.300 position:92%
of the rules that I lived by, the things that I believe in.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:45.420 position:84%
I couldn't do that, and I would've rather walked away,

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.833 position:84%
but I didn't, I did it instead, and look where we are.

00:06:48.833 --> 00:06:49.920
To earn the title

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.810 position:59%
of the world's greenest football club,

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:55.320 position:78%
FGR have done much more than just change the menu.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.830 position:72%
The stadium is solely powered by green energy;

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.570
the pitch itself is organic,

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.970 position:58%
free from pesticides and weed killer,

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:06.660 position:59%
fed by seaweed and captured rainwater.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.603 position:66%
It's also cut with a solar powered Mowbot.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.240
For electric car drivers,

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.990
they can charge up during the game.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.373 position:58%
I think it permeates to a huge level.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.430 position:70%
It's a little bit of thinking out of the box.

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:23.826 position:91%
It's just trying to think about things in a different way,

00:07:23.826 --> 00:07:25.770
not the way it's always been done.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.653 position:59%
Well, it's just a passion that I have,

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.810 position:59%
to see us get to a place where we live

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:31.890
in a more sustainable way.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.690 position:70%
We're not wasting stuff, not polluting stuff,

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:37.443 position:89%
not wiping out nature and not causing the climate crisis.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:43.020 position:70%
The players and staff can eat what they want,

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.810 position:64%
but when at work, training, or match day,

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.973
there's only vegan food served.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.140 position:88%
Wingback Kane Wilson, the league's player of the season,

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:55.170 position:86%
is one of an increasing number of professional athletes

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.883
who are turning away from meat.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.160
I had an injury, tendonitis,

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.733 position:72%
which is like an injury that was inflammatory,

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.490 position:64%
and was in my knee, and I was struggling.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:07.080 position:70%
I tried everything to get rid of this injury,

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:10.170 line:0%
I couldn't shake it, and it was costing me money,

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.130 size:78% position:39% line:0%
because I wasn't playing,

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.980 line:0%
so I had to try and find a way to get rid of it.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:15.510
I was gonna go for an operation,

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.040 position:63%
I was thinking of all different options,

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.470 position:70%
and I just seen an athlete in America talking

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.360
about how he had suffered from it

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.140 position:58%
and changed his diet and it had gone,

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:27.150 position:89%
so I said, well, that's what I've gotta do now, isn't it?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.493 position:58%
I mean, it worked for me, hands down.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.820 position:61%
A large number of high profile athletes

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.950
extol the benefits of going vegan,

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.770 position:70%
from sports as diverse as tennis, basketball,

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:41.430 position:72%
ultra marathon racing, and even body building.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.110
Some at Forest Green are convinced

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:45.780 position:75%
their vegan only food rule might be contributing

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.700
to their recent success.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.810
The team hasn't dropped out

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:51.003
of the top three places all season.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.090 position:70%
So does playing for the world's greenest club

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.400
change anything for a player?

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.140 position:78%
It probably just rewires you a little bit in terms

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:01.770 position:86%
of maybe things that you wasn't as conscious of before.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:02.603
It's everything.

00:09:03.477 --> 00:09:05.520 position:67%
It's everything involved with Forest Green.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:06.870
I didn't even know it was possible

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.420 position:61%
for a t-shirt to be made out of coffee.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.943
I didn't know that was a thing.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.740
What's perhaps most remarkable

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:16.920 position:66%
is how far the Forest Green ethos reaches,

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.900
far beyond the few thousand people

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.240
of local village, Nailsworth.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.220 position:64%
Welcome to the "Heaven's Devils" podcast,

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.580 position:72%
a Forest Green Rovers podcast by two Americans

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.950 position:69%
who have no idea what they're talking about.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:31.500 position:63%
Yeah, so we were brought in by the vegan

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.020
and green aspects of the club.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:39.020 line:0%
It matched our personal ethics, and so we found this club

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.007 position:64%
that is doing so much good off the pitch,

00:09:41.007 --> 00:09:42.420 position:73%
and we were like, if we're gonna give our money

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:45.213 position:86%
and our time to a team, let's do it to a team that is--

00:09:45.213 --> 00:09:46.380
That matters.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:47.490
That matters. Just like The Clash

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:49.080
are the only band that matters,

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.303 position:67%
for us, FGR are the only club that matters.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.870 position:72%
Nathan and Shyam have made it over from the US

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.663 position:81%
for a critical game in Forest Green Rovers' history.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:01.290
It's the end of April, 2022,

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.300 position:63%
and with four games to go of the season,

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:06.360 position:81%
a draw away at Bristol Rovers would secure promotion

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:07.320
to the league above.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.790
Promotion, that's all I want.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.560
One point will do.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:11.460
True to form,

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.110 position:59%
the greenest club in the world arrives

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:16.290 position:69%
on an electric bus, something the club hopes

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:18.453 position:63%
to make a permanent fixture next season.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:23.370 position:77%
Dale is in relaxed mood, happy to see a vegan pie

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:24.573
on another club's menu.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.660
Vegan pie of the month.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.171
How often do you see that away?

00:10:29.171 --> 00:10:30.255
Oh, you know what?

00:10:30.255 --> 00:10:32.261
It's quite common now.

00:10:32.261 --> 00:10:33.094
It's amazing.

00:10:33.094 --> 00:10:35.183
We went Carlisle a few months ago,

00:10:35.183 --> 00:10:38.369 position:56%
and they had two kinds of vegan pie.

00:10:42.052 --> 00:10:43.580
Leading the way for the majority

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.153
of the season, Forest Green.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.423 position:59%
